## Planned regressions

Planned regression: workflow gate read_checkout true parse and encode round-trip.

Planned regression: workflow gate absent and false omit read_checkout and retain
the output-only zero value.

Planned regression: GateAttempt read_checkout true JSON round-trip.

Planned regression: GateAttempt false omits read_checkout while legacy gate JSON
still parses.

Every encode assertion pins an independent inline YAML or JSON literal rather
than deriving its oracle with the production encoder. Round-trip equality alone
is insufficient because matching encode/decode mistakes can agree with each
other.

## L2 author declarations

TOPOLOGY: no concurrency change; pure in-memory schema decode, validate, and
encode at the existing single call sites.

DURABILITY CLASS: no irreversible action and no delivery operation. The change
adds an optional leaf field to workflow YAML and manifest JSON; existing git CAS
writes remain unchanged.

COMPLETE SET / all-sites enumeration: the complete representation set is four
sites — workflow domain model, workflow YAML codec, manifest domain model, and
manifest JSON codec — plus one focused test surface for each codec. No other
serializer exists for either type.

TRUST BOUNDARY: workflow YAML and manifest JSON are untrusted parsed inputs;
`yaml.v3` KnownFields and `json.Decoder.DisallowUnknownFields` are the validation
roots. The typed boolean is trusted after successful decode. Arbitrary
same-process code execution is outside scope.

IRREVERSIBLE SEQUENCES: none

